    q: "A CI/CD pipeline's deploy service account currently has full admin access to the cloud account, but only ever creates/updates resources in one specific S3 bucket and one Lambda function. What's the fix?",
    sol: "Create a scoped IAM role/policy granting only the specific actions needed (s3:PutObject on that bucket's ARN, lambda:UpdateFunctionCode on that function's ARN) and attach that to the deploy service account instead of admin access. Review and re-scope the policy whenever the pipeline's actual responsibilities change.",
    exp: "A compromised CI credential with admin access can compromise the entire cloud account; a properly scoped one limits the damage to exactly what that pipeline needed to do anyway.",
