    q: "You're adding a 'export my data to CSV' feature. Do a quick STRIDE pass and name one concrete risk per applicable category.",
    sol: "Spoofing: is the export request tied to an authenticated session, or could a forged request trigger it for another user? Tampering: could the export parameters be manipulated to include another user's data? Information Disclosure: does the export accidentally include fields that shouldn't leave the system (internal IDs, other users' data via a join bug)? Denial of Service: could requesting many large exports concurrently exhaust server resources? Elevation of Privilege: not directly applicable unless the export endpoint also grants any write capability.",
    exp: "STRIDE forces a systematic pass across categories instead of only thinking about the one risk that happens to come to mind first.",
