    sol: "The support tool is arguably higher-risk than the main login since a single compromised agent account gives an attacker broad access to all customers' PII, not just one account's data. Next steps: prioritize MFA rollout to any tool granting broad/privileged access first, not just customer-facing logins, and audit for any other internal tool with similarly broad access still relying on password-only auth.",
    exp: "MFA rollouts often focus on the most visible surface (customer login) while leaving higher-blast-radius internal tools under-protected — prioritize by access breadth, not visibility.",
