    q: "A company's e-commerce database can tolerate at most 15 minutes of lost transaction data and must be back online within 1 hour of an outage. Translate this into concrete backup/DR requirements.",
    sol: "RPO of 15 minutes requires continuous/near-continuous replication or transaction-log backups at least every 15 minutes (a nightly full backup alone gives an RPO of up to 24 hours — far too coarse). RTO of 1 hour requires either a warm standby replica that can be promoted quickly, or automated, tested restore tooling — a manual restore process that takes hours to execute by hand won't meet a 1-hour RTO regardless of how good the backups themselves are.",
    exp: "RPO drives backup FREQUENCY; RTO drives how fast RESTORATION can actually happen — they're independent requirements that both need explicit engineering, not just 'we have backups.'",
