    q: "A support tool logs full customer support chat transcripts, including messages where customers paste their credit card number to 'verify' a payment issue, into a general-purpose logging system with broad internal access. Identify the compliance/security problem and the fix.",
    sol: "This is a PCI-DSS violation risk (storing unmasked cardholder data outside a properly scoped, access-controlled cardholder data environment) and a data-minimization failure — broad internal access to logs containing full card numbers massively expands the exposure if any of those accounts/systems is compromised. Fix: implement automated redaction/masking of card-number patterns before logging (a regex-based scrubber at the logging pipeline level), and train support staff to never ask customers to paste full card numbers in chat at all.",
