    sol: "Command & Control and Exfiltration are strong picks: even if reconnaissance, delivery, and initial exploitation all succeed (which is common — perimeter prevention is never 100%), detecting C2 traffic or unusual outbound data transfer still stops the attack before the actual damage (data theft/ransomware detonation) occurs. Investing only in perimeter-stage detection (reconnaissance/delivery) means a single successful bypass of those early stages goes fully undetected for everything after.",
    exp: "Detection coverage concentrated only at the earliest kill-chain stages creates a single point of total blindness once an attacker gets past them — later-stage detections provide a second (and often more decisive) chance to catch an intrusion already in progress.",
