    q: "A Node API validates JWTs like this: const decoded = jwt.decode(token); if (decoded.role === 'admin') { ... } — no signature verification at all. Identify every problem and fix it.",
    sol: "jwt.decode() only base64-decodes the payload without verifying the signature — anyone can craft a token with role: 'admin' in the payload and it will be accepted, since nothing checks whether it was actually signed by the server. Fix: use jwt.verify(token, secretOrPublicKey, { algorithms: ['HS256'] }) — explicitly pinning the expected algorithm(s) server-side (never trusting the token's own alg header) — and only trust claims from a token that passes verification.",
