    q: "An e-commerce 'apply coupon' endpoint checks coupon.usesRemaining > 0, then separately decrements it in a follow-up query. A user manages to redeem a one-time coupon 4 times by firing 4 concurrent requests. Diagnose and fix.",
    sol: "Classic TOCTOU race condition: all 4 concurrent requests read usesRemaining=1 (check) before any of them commits the decrement (use), so all 4 pass the check. Fix: make the check-and-decrement atomic at the database level, e.g. UPDATE coupons SET uses_remaining = uses_remaining - 1 WHERE id = ? AND uses_remaining > 0, then check the affected-row count — if 0 rows were updated, the coupon was already exhausted, and only requests that actually succeed in decrementing get the discount applied.",
