    sol: "Combining no rate limiting with an expensive, attacker-controlled regex parameter is a resource-exhaustion DoS vector — a maliciously crafted 'evil regex' (catastrophic backtracking) can consume server CPU disproportionately relative to a tiny request, and with no rate limiting an attacker can send many such requests rapidly. Add: per-IP rate limiting even for unauthenticated endpoints, a regex complexity/timeout guard (or better, disallow raw regex input entirely and offer only a fixed set of search modes), and monitoring for anomalous request latency/CPU spend per endpoint.",
